  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elbit Systems of America Night Vision obligated $323M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The company won 113 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.9M and obligations up 8.4% year over year. Commercial and Service Industry Machinery Manufacturing is the dominant market, accounting for $294M of obligations in FY2026 to date. The company also recorded obligations in Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $24M and smaller amounts in Manufacturing and Reproducing Magnetic and Optical Media at $2.6M. Historical obligations show growth from $31.5M in FY21 to $323M in FY26, with notable steps at $119M in FY22 and $270M in FY24. Contracts range across specialized manufacturing niches, including Hardware Manufacturing at $1.1M and Audio and Video Equipment Manufacturing at $327K. The current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. Use these figures to size market exposure, compare award frequency, and prioritize outreach into the largest NAICS markets where obligations concentrate.",
    "sections": [
